<%# ID-7: Privacy (DEV_GUIDE §5, text as written). -%>
<article class="card prose">
  <p><strong>What we store:</strong> your university e-mail address; your password as a bcrypt hash (nobody can read it); your handle, avatar, bio and settings; the posts, comments and private messages you write and the images you upload; the posts you like and watch; the posts you open, and when (your history, which you can clear); and the reports you file.</p>
  <p><strong>Who sees what:</strong> on an anonymous post, other users see no handle, and on every post commenters appear under an alias such as Host or Alice. Your handle is shown only on posts where you turn on "Show my handle", on your public page, and in private conversations started from your page. Your e-mail address is shown only to you (on your Profile) and to the admins. Admins can see who wrote a post or comment when they deal with a report, so that they can act on abuse.</p>
  <p><strong>E-mail:</strong> we only send you sign-up and password-reset codes.</p>
  <p><strong>Where it runs:</strong> Campus Notes is a course demo that runs locally on the team's own computers. The data is not sold or shared with anyone, the demo database is reset often, and it is deleted after the course.</p>
</article>
